WEBVTT

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:04.920
Is this news report about the Coupling
system being used in Chitose accurate?

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.400
Its development was supposedly prohibited.

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:09.900
Where did they get their funding from?

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:18.160
Wasn't it unveiled at a good time?

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:25.170
To change the tide of war, the tiger must eventually make its way out of its cage.

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:31.820
Regardless of what the assembly decides,
there are plenty of others who will support us.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:33.880
Are you sure the citizens will side with us?

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:37.220
I've got everything under control.

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:43.730
I'm supposed to wear a swimsuit?!

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:46.060
I'm saying that it's a possibility.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:49.360
The main shots will be of Luxon and Bradyon,

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:52.520
but they also want shots of the crew and the inside of the ship.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:54.030
Please hold on.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:01:01.880
The top brass not only made us fly to the Hawaii
base independently through unsecured airspace,

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:03.870
but they're also asking us to act?

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:07.610
If they'll forgive us that easily, then why not?

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:09.650
That may be so, but…

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:12.800
We're on the final approach.

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:20.720
About the promotional video...

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:24.100
We're in the middle of a war.
Is this really the right time for that, Jarl-san?

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.060
They're making one precisely <i>because</i> we're in the middle of a war.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:29.320
It will help recruit more soldiers and increase the budget.

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:31.570
Well, it's really complicated.

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:33.570
Unlike what's in your head.

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:35.470
What's that supposed to mean?

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:37.800
Anyway, do you understand?

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:42.580
Since the promotional video is about the
Coupling System, you and Dio will have the lead roles.

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:43.910
Huh? Me?

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:48.670
Whether the Alliance wins or loses might depend on how photogenic you are.

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:50.180
Wait...

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:51.580
Hold on. It's all too sudden.

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:55.920
Oh! These are Luxon and Bradyon? They're great!

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:57.930
Whoa! Second Lieutenant Weinberg!

00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:02.140
That rumor about him being one of the most
handsome pilots in the Alliance is not just for show.

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:04.720
So, you're Watase Aoba-kun?

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:07.230
I-I'm new, but I'll do my best.

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:10.690
Sorry. You're not gonna be on camera this time.

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:11.650
Eh?

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:15.900
We've brought another Coupler for Dio-kun, you see.

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:18.150
Isn't that a Beryl Explorer?

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:20.910
It's been a long time, Dio!

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:23.660
Fromm... is that you?!

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:25.810
Hey there. How have you been?

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:32.050
I'm Ensign Fromm Vantarhei.
I'm here as the Coupler for the promotional video.

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:34.250
Hey. I'm Jarl Duran.

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:37.210
Sorry about this, Aoba-kun.

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:40.930
I'll have to borrow your Luxon for a while.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:44.210
My Beryl isn't capable of Coupling, you see.

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:45.680
O-Okay...

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:51.370
I heard you had a "Nice Coupling" with Dio,
even without preliminary adjustments.

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:52.310
Amazing.

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:54.150
Is that so?

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:57.290
You've got to tell me more of your story later.

00:02:57.290 --> 00:02:58.360
My story?

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:00.860
Yep. You have a unique profile, right?

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:04.120
Ah, sort of.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.040
Spread your wings

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:14.670
See the light of hope in the sky you have yet to witness

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:17.970
And don't ever give in to the weight of sorrow

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:23.350
Echo unto eternity, "Unisonia"

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:32.610
That world you see before your eyes

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:38.240
I wonder what colors it is made of

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.660
The pain of loss isn't something

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:45.620
You want to get used to, and yet

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:50.580
Even on a night like this, the stars glisten

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:57.550
Like a tarnished coin spilling from the palm of your hand

00:03:57.840 --> 00:03:59.380
Can't go back

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:00.800
Want to go home

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:04.140
The two of them back-to-back

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:06.180
Break through

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:10.940
Turning unfading emotions into a lasting bond

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:14.270
Like painting over a colorless world

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:17.020
Let this sympathy reach

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:23.240
Let's build the future that we envision

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:26.450
You'll see, we'll even change fate

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:31.250
Transcending time, "Unisonia"

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:42.130
The red doors indicate dangerous areas and the purple
doors indicate classified areas, so they're both off-limits.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:43.960
In addition, the ship is...

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:44.430
What is it?

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:48.580
The crew of the Cygnus are truly fortunate.

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:52.390
They get to share life and death experiences
with such a beautiful officer as yourself.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:53.810
What?

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:03.470
Since the ship is currently involved in an operation,
there's no telling when we may be engaged in battle...

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:06.070
That's more than I could ask for!

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:11.680
Only in a battle between life and death can I get the best shots.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.700
I'm counting on you, Fromm! You too, Dio-kun!

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:16.210
I'm happy to fly together once again.

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:18.170
Yeah, sure.

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:25.090
Did you hear? The other pilot for the Coupling
System promotional video is a handsome guy.

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:26.040
I've heard.

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:27.340
Oh, that's a surprise.

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:30.400
I thought you weren't interested in those kinds of things.

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:31.720
Of course not.

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:38.690
I'm interested in what kinds of brain waves he has or how his Sympathy Spectrum changes course.

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:40.220
I see.

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:43.570
Well, you already have your Watase Aoba.

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:44.100
What?

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:46.900
Okay. Let's go.

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:48.680
Where to?

00:05:50.170 --> 00:05:52.240
To feast our eyes.

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:55.750
We want to do location scouting before the shoot.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:57.250
Can we get your permission?

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:00.750
<i>A handsome guy!</i>

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:02.840
Well then, I'll have a soldier show you around.

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:04.960
Me! Please let me do it!

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:05.840
Corporal?

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:11.010
My name's Anessa Rossetti. Aside from being your guide,
if you have any issues, feel free to ask me anything!

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:14.970
I'm delighted to have a cute girl look after me.

00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:17.310
Come on.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:22.090
Oh yeah, would it be alright to let her be
the facilitator for the promotional video?

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:24.820
That's great, Fromm. We can do that.

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:25.600
Is that okay with you?

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:26.590
Of course!

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:26.890
Dio?

00:06:26.890 --> 00:06:28.280
It's decided, then.

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:31.170
See you later, Dio.

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:35.790
So, where do you wanna go first?

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:38.290
How about the bridge?

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:42.960
He an acquaintance of yours?

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:45.380
That guy Fromm.

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:47.260
Yeah.

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:48.770
What's he like?

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:53.930
Lake Louis?

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:56.290
It's a Coupler training facility.

00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:58.180
We were in the same class.

00:06:58.180 --> 00:06:59.520
I see.

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:05.850
He had top grades in all academic and practical classes,
using both simulators or real machines.

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:07.230
Is that so?

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:10.700
And he seems like a good guy to me.

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:13.060
He's good at socializing.

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:16.450
I always remember seeing him surrounded by people.

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:18.540
The total opposite of you.

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:23.140
It's a trait that's unnecessary for a soldier.

00:07:23.140 --> 00:07:25.360
But he was an excellent student, wasn't he?

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:30.210
I can't bring myself to like shallow-minded people.

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:33.720
And nosy people as well.

00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:37.220
You mean me?

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:43.040
Currently, it seems that Chitose has
not dispatched any units to pursue us.

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:46.860
It's not that easy to neutralize the enemy territory.

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:51.240
Their hands are probably full with organizing a framework.

00:07:56.690 --> 00:07:59.250
Regarding our rendezvous at the Hawaii base...

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:00.620
Wh-What are you doing?

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:03.790
Nothing. Please don't mind me.

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:06.790
Basil?

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:11.260
The disguise and deployment tests were completed yesterday.

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:13.260
It will be arriving shortly.

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:15.970
We'll be outfitted with such a new machine?

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:21.430
The Commanders of the National Armed Forces were quite
impressed by your efforts in the capture of Chitose Base.

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:24.450
"As expected of Alfried Gallant."

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:26.490
It's my pleasure.

00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:28.980
You performed this much distinguished service for us.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:32.040
The Administration Bureau had no complaints.

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:37.700
However, I doubt that they're
just going to sit back and watch.

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:42.730
At the very least, I hope that they will not get in our way.

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:55.220
<i>They're still suspicious of me.</i>

00:08:56.840 --> 00:09:00.560
<i>Why didn't that new-type fight back?</i>

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:02.930
<i>It's me! Watase Aoba!</i>

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:05.560
<i>That pilot…</i>

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:06.720
<i>What on Earth?</i>

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:10.820
Hina, are you there?

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:11.730
Lasha?

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:15.730
Come here quickly.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:20.160
Thank goodness, they're still around.

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:23.620
They're cute, aren't they?

00:09:24.820 --> 00:09:25.710
Yes.

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:30.790
Yeah, deer are good.

00:09:30.790 --> 00:09:34.340
Especially the fawn; it'd be delicious with tomato sauce.

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:35.010
What?!

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:38.840
Well then, I'll go borrow a rifle.

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:42.970
No, Tarjim! It's not meant for that.

00:09:45.990 --> 00:09:47.870
It's good to see you in high spirits again.

00:09:51.550 --> 00:09:54.280
Let's start the reel. Ready!

00:09:55.850 --> 00:10:01.240
These are the Coupling Valiancers, Luxon and Bradyon.

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:07.410
Well then, let's talk to the maintenance chief Don Naher.

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:11.380
Do they have any problems that normal Valiancers don't have?

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:17.770
Well, I'd say "To be interrupted of important duties by some easy-going idiots."

00:10:17.770 --> 00:10:19.840
I see.

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:20.810
I knew it.

00:10:20.810 --> 00:10:26.340
You must pay special attention to the balance and
nutrition of the meals of Coupling Valiancer pilots, right?

00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:30.770
I pay attention to the meals of every soldier, you know?

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:33.570
O-Of course!

00:10:33.890 --> 00:10:36.030
After a hard day's work,
there's always a need for a short break.

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:39.780
This is the best spot to refresh both your mind and body.

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:42.740
This is good. So sexy. I'll take it!

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:43.900
You're the best!

00:10:43.900 --> 00:10:45.080
Thank you!

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:48.080
Fools.

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:53.250
The Imperial Guard?

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:56.720
This plan will show the power of the Administration Bureau to all the citizens of Zogilia.

00:10:56.720 --> 00:11:00.510
And at the same time, it will take the
prestige of the military down a notch.

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:01.890
Almost like killing two birds with one stone.

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:04.180
As expected of you, Vice-Minister Gille.

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:09.600
Your report on Alfried Gallant's unit and all the battle information with those men was sent to Gavarock.

00:11:09.990 --> 00:11:17.110
When we see successful results,
you'll be rewarded accordingly.

00:11:17.960 --> 00:11:19.820
Glory to Zogilia.

00:11:31.090 --> 00:11:35.620
Now is the time to show the power of the Imperial Guards, under the direct control of the Administrative Bureau.

00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:40.490
The foolish Alliance's new-type is not enough to scare us.

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:42.840
Ready for battle, Sir Dolzief!

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:43.720
All right.

00:11:44.530 --> 00:11:45.780
Well then, let's go!

00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:47.220
Yes, sir!

00:12:02.270 --> 00:12:05.530
Both of their Emphater levels are unstable.

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:09.800
Does that mean Fromm and Dio-kun can't do Coupling?

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:11.640
I can't safely permit it at this level.

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:12.830
Wait.
What?

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:18.300
When we were tested at Lake Louis,
Fromm and I had a "Nice Coupling" reaction.

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:22.300
We had the best compatibility among the freshmen.

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:27.260
Dio, your Emphater wave has changed since then.

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:29.260
My wave has changed?

00:12:29.260 --> 00:12:32.730
Yes, it's way off from the baseline wave.

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:33.850
That can't be.

00:12:34.150 --> 00:12:35.220
The cause?

00:12:35.220 --> 00:12:36.980
I can't say for sure now.

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:40.150
Is it because of real-life battle experiences?

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:42.490
We can't rule out that possibility.

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:45.130
Whatever. What about the filming?

00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:47.240
Excuse me. I have an idea.

00:12:48.060 --> 00:12:49.070
What is it?

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:55.870
From debut actor to a camera assistant, that's quite a promotion, kid.

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:57.960
Not you too, Don-san.

00:12:57.960 --> 00:13:00.670
Ensign Watase, report to the observation room at once.

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:02.920
I repeat, Ensign Watase...

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:16.520
This can't be.

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:17.680
Amazing.

00:13:17.680 --> 00:13:19.440
What are these readings?

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:23.000
What a great match for a first Coupling test.

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:24.280
Yeah...

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:25.820
So how is it?

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:27.990
Can they or can't they?

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:28.870
Elvira.

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:31.580
The readings indicate no problems.

00:13:33.490 --> 00:13:34.370
You have my permission.

00:13:34.370 --> 00:13:38.830
Well then, we'll swap out Dio-kun for
the shots filmed inside the cockpit.

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:42.050
I'll go with Fromm Coupling with Aoba-kun!

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:43.550
Wh-What?

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:45.260
Best regards.

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:47.260
Best regards?

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:49.120
What do you mean?

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:58.270
<i>We'll be launching each Valiancer for public relations duty.</i>

00:13:58.270 --> 00:14:00.940
<i>I repeat, public relations duty.</i>

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:06.240
<i>In order to switch the Coupler,
we'll be changing the pilot assignments.</i>

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:08.800
Luxon will be Ensign Watase Aoba.

00:14:08.800 --> 00:14:09.740
Okay!

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:14.780
Bradyon will be Ensign Fromm Vantarhei
substituting for Ensign Dio Weinberg.

00:14:14.780 --> 00:14:18.080
Don't hold back just because this is your first time Buddying with me.

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:19.880
Alright. Leave it to me!

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:23.380
Ensign Weinberg will be in a Beryl.

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:28.200
<i>Real-life combat experiences, huh?</i>

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:31.800
<i>I can't believe they affect the Emphater Waveform.</i>

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:33.960
<i>If that's the case, then why only me?</i>

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:36.640
Cheer up, Dio.

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:38.360
There are days like this.

00:14:38.360 --> 00:14:41.690
That's right. Don't mind it, camera assistant!

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:43.060
Don't go overboard.

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:49.700
Good. Good, Luxon!

00:14:50.010 --> 00:14:52.950
I'm counting on you for those big action sequences.

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:06.210
Well then, let's begin, Aoba-kun!

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:08.280
Okay. Let's do it!

00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:10.470
Connect with Fromm!

00:15:10.780 --> 00:15:11.970
Accept!

00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:20.980
This is much stronger than
Aoba-san's first Coupling with Dio.

00:15:22.170 --> 00:15:23.730
Yeah...

00:15:46.530 --> 00:15:48.510
Aoba-kun is really amazing.

00:15:48.780 --> 00:15:49.460
What?

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:52.800
Even without any Coupling training, he's still able to perform well.

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:01.100
<i>Such amazing speed.</i>

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:13.490
<i>It might've been a coincidence when it was only with me.</i>

00:16:14.210 --> 00:16:17.410
<i>However, even with Fromm for the first time...</i>

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:19.170
<i>What in the world is he?</i>

00:16:23.770 --> 00:16:24.620
Break.

00:16:30.330 --> 00:16:32.920
There's a large number of Valiancers approaching from the rear!

00:16:32.920 --> 00:16:35.130
Get First Lieutenant Duran ready to launch.

00:16:35.130 --> 00:16:35.680
Yes!

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:37.300
Are they from Chitose?

00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:39.940
We're unable to determine their origin.

00:16:39.940 --> 00:16:41.570
Well then, where are they from?

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:44.060
I'm bringing up the feed from Beryl E's camera.

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:46.150
That mecha...

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:54.740
Those are the new-types that forced us, the Imperial Guards, to make our move.

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:56.320
Remember what you've been briefed on.

00:16:56.320 --> 00:16:58.280
Get the white swan's attention.

00:16:58.280 --> 00:16:59.280
Yes, sir!

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:04.160
Be careful.

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:06.600
They are the Elite Guards from Zogilia's headquarters.

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:07.580
Seriously?

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:11.960
Looks like they're planning to completely destroy the Coupling System.

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:18.610
Damn it.

00:17:18.610 --> 00:17:20.600
I have to fight them in a Beryl.

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:25.970
Aren't those the Imperial Guards?!

00:17:25.970 --> 00:17:27.850
They finally made their move!

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:29.860
Give me a break!

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:33.570
Damn it!

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:47.460
You won't get away!

00:17:48.630 --> 00:17:49.500
What?

00:17:50.930 --> 00:17:54.930
It's only their first Coupling so they
can't fight to the best of their abilities.

00:17:54.930 --> 00:17:57.840
Their Emphater Level is terrifying.

00:17:57.840 --> 00:18:01.440
If they're struggling, that means the enemy is much stronger.

00:18:08.850 --> 00:18:09.420
Dammit.

00:18:09.420 --> 00:18:11.820
As you'd expect of the Imperial Guards.
They've got no openings!

00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:21.700
Aerial Mines, huh? Get me a safe route!

00:18:23.910 --> 00:18:25.160
I can't manuever well.

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:29.710
Damn. I can't get out.

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:31.460
This way?

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:36.380
This is the only way.

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:38.380
If I can break out this way...

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:47.480
It can't be...

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:49.310
Are they driving Luxon there?

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:51.150
I can't cover him!

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:55.730
Aoba!

00:18:57.780 --> 00:18:59.280
Dammit!

00:18:59.980 --> 00:19:01.530
Weakling.

00:19:07.230 --> 00:19:10.920
You think you can defeat us with just speed and maneuverability?

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:13.960
Are they luring him into the line of fire?!

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:16.380
I won't let you!

00:19:24.180 --> 00:19:24.640
What?!

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:37.690
What was that?!

00:19:49.410 --> 00:19:52.370
That stock mass-produced Alliance mecha.

00:19:52.370 --> 00:19:53.580
Should we pursue?

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:57.920
Since our enclosure formation has been broken, we need to re-think our strategy.

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:03.590
The enemy is retreating.

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:06.550
Yes! I've got the best shots.

00:20:07.050 --> 00:20:09.140
The best. The best!

00:20:09.780 --> 00:20:11.810
They'll be back, I suppose.

00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:14.310
Yes. We'll be on alert.

00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:29.080
You drove the enemy back with only a Beryl? Not bad.

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:31.330
Thank you, you saved me.

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:33.430
You really are great.

00:20:34.420 --> 00:20:35.960
It's my mission.

00:20:36.830 --> 00:20:38.880
They're back!

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:43.340
Nothing is more convincing than the
shots of a life and death battle, after all.

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:46.080
That said, this will be the last shot.

00:20:53.620 --> 00:20:55.650
Now, are you all ready?

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:58.110
Okay. Let's do this!

00:20:59.080 --> 00:21:02.110
Five, four, three...

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:06.700
Come on, you and me.

00:21:07.180 --> 00:21:08.770
Let's Coupling.

00:21:09.490 --> 00:21:10.990
Alright! Okay!

00:21:10.990 --> 00:21:12.950
Good job!

00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:14.660
Well done.

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:18.420
This take is okay. Now send it in for editing.

00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:25.130
After replenishing our supplies, we'll resume the attacks.

00:21:25.130 --> 00:21:27.480
Don't give them any room to breathe!

00:21:27.480 --> 00:21:28.640
Yes, sir!

00:21:29.550 --> 00:21:34.100
<i>I see. For Alfried Gallant to have difficulties is understandable.</i>

00:21:34.100 --> 00:21:36.990
<i>But it won't be the same next time.</i>

00:21:37.830 --> 00:21:41.650
The Alliance's new-type... will soon be in my hands.

00:21:42.300 --> 00:21:44.400
They're gone.

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:46.940
So even you can make a face like that.

00:21:46.940 --> 00:21:47.780
Which one?

00:21:48.110 --> 00:21:49.740
"Let's Coupling."

00:21:51.310 --> 00:21:52.990
It's my mission.

00:21:53.340 --> 00:21:55.640
That guy is really nice.

00:21:55.640 --> 00:21:58.410
It would've been nicer if he had stayed longer.

00:21:58.410 --> 00:21:59.400
Not really.

00:21:59.400 --> 00:22:01.460
Don't say such cold things, Dio.

00:22:01.460 --> 00:22:05.370
Huh? But didn't the film crew just leave?

00:22:06.380 --> 00:22:07.480
Fromm!

00:22:07.480 --> 00:22:10.590
Is it true that you've been assigned to the Cygnus?

00:22:11.810 --> 00:22:15.170
Huh? Didn't I tell you guys?

00:22:15.170 --> 00:22:15.180
With my heart, I call out
Huh? Didn't I tell you guys?

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:18.920
With my heart, I call out

00:22:18.920 --> 00:22:23.300
To the far side, mutually drawn

00:22:23.300 --> 00:22:27.810
Forgetting even the reason I ache

00:22:27.810 --> 00:22:32.440
Just for now, please

00:22:32.440 --> 00:22:36.610
I know you

00:22:36.610 --> 00:22:41.110
I'm searching for you

00:22:41.240 --> 00:22:43.570
Softly pressing my lips

00:22:43.570 --> 00:22:50.210
to the bright afterimage I can't keep from leaving

00:22:50.210 --> 00:22:58.760
If hesitation is what gives way to the slightest of hopes

00:22:58.760 --> 00:23:03.340
To the many gentle mornings...

00:23:03.340 --> 00:23:07.890
and the times I have wondered

00:23:07.890 --> 00:23:12.140
In the future that leads back to that sky,

00:23:12.140 --> 00:23:14.400
I want to save you,

00:23:14.400 --> 00:23:16.480
I want to protect you

00:23:16.480 --> 00:23:20.860
In the future that arrives at that dream

00:23:20.860 --> 00:23:23.740
Wait for me

00:23:23.740 --> 00:23:28.490
The love we'll surely find

00:23:28.490 --> 00:23:33.290
I want you to reach out for it

00:23:36.090 --> 00:23:38.430
Next episode, on Buddy Complex:

00:23:38.430 --> 00:23:39.530
"Buddy."
